# Local mock service

The  service is an explicitly opt-in Compose profile. It uses a locally built Python image and the built-in HTTP handler; it does not call external services and has no published host port, bind mount, named volume, or Docker socket. Its  network is marked .

The default worker remains isolated with  and has no mounts, so it cannot reach this mock. The mock profile is a fixture for local healthcheck/response demonstrations, not an egress path or authorization bypass.

Start only the mock profile when specifically needed:



Do not attach the worker to  or publish the mock port.
